@startuml
skinparam lifelineStrategy solid
autonumber
title Diagrama Devoluciones 7: POST /api/v1/refunds/:id/levels/current/reject (Rechazar el nivel activo)

actor "Aprobador del nivel" as Approver
participant "App Web" as Web
participant "Gateway Controller" as Gateway
participant "Refund Workflow Service" as Service
participant "Transaction Manager\n(QueryRunner)" as TX
participant "refund_orders DB" as OrdersDB
participant "refund_workflow_instances DB" as InstanceDB
participant "refund_workflow_instance_levels DB" as LevelsDB
participant "refund_workflow_actions DB" as ActionsDB

Approver -> Web: Tap en "Rechazar" + motivo obligatorio
Web -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/refunds/2001/levels/current/reject\n(RejectLevelDto: { reason, comment })
Gateway -> Service: rejectCurrentLevel(refundOrderId: 2001, payload, actor)

Service -> OrdersDB: 1. findRefundOrderWithInstance(2001)
OrdersDB --> Service: order + instance { id: 90, status: 'IN_APPROVAL' }

Service -> LevelsDB: 2. findCurrentLevel(90)
LevelsDB --> Service: level { id: 201, level_order: 2,\nrole_code, on_reject: 'TERMINATE' }

Service -> Service: 3. assertCanReject(order, level, actor, payload)
note right of Service
  422 si falta reason: en REJECT es obligatorio
  403 si el actor no pertenece al rol del nivel
  409 si la instancia no está IN_APPROVAL
end note

Service -> TX: 4. startTransaction()
activate TX

Service -> LevelsDB: 5. closeLevel(201, 'REJECTED', finishedAt: NOW())
LevelsDB --> Service: ok

Service -> ActionsDB: 6. insertWorkflowAction(90, 201, 'REJECT')
note right of ActionsDB
  - reason obligatorio
  - comment del revisor
  - previous_status = 'IN_APPROVAL'
end note
ActionsDB --> Service: ok

alt on_reject = 'TERMINATE'
    Service -> InstanceDB: 7. closeInstance(90, 'REJECTED', currentLevelOrder: NULL, finishedAt: NOW())
    InstanceDB --> Service: ok

    Service -> OrdersDB: 8. updateRefundOrderStatus(2001, 'REJECTED')
    note right of OrdersDB
      La nota muere acá. Reabrirla exige
      una REACTIVATE explícita, que crea
      un intento nuevo.
    end note
    OrdersDB --> Service: ok

    Service -> ActionsDB: 9. insertWorkflowAction(90, NULL, 'CLOSED')
    ActionsDB --> Service: ok
else on_reject = 'RETURN_PREVIOUS'
    Service -> LevelsDB: 10. reopenPreviousLevel(90, level_order - 1)
    note right of LevelsDB
      El nivel anterior vuelve a IN_PROGRESS
      con started_at = NOW() y finished_at = NULL.
      La instancia sigue IN_APPROVAL.
    end note
    LevelsDB --> Service: previousLevelId

    Service -> InstanceDB: 11. updateCurrentLevelOrder(90, level_order - 1)
    InstanceDB --> Service: ok
else on_reject = 'RETURN_INITIATOR'
    Service -> LevelsDB: 12. resetPendingLevels(90)
    note right of LevelsDB
      Todos los niveles del intento
      quedan PENDING: la nota vuelve al
      vendedor para corregirla.
    end note
    LevelsDB --> Service: ok

    Service -> InstanceDB: 13. updateInstance(90, 'EDITING', currentLevelOrder: NULL)
    note right of InstanceDB
      La nota queda editable. El vendedor
      corrige cantidades y la reenvía
      (SELLER_RESUBMITTED), sin volver a
      seleccionar ítems.
    end note
    InstanceDB --> Service: ok
end

Service -> TX: 14. commitTransaction()
deactivate TX

Service --> Gateway: 200 OK (RejectLevelResult:\n{ orderStatus, instanceStatus, currentLevelOrder, onReject })
Gateway --> Web: 200 OK
Web --> Approver: Rechazo registrado • Destino según la política del nivel
@enduml
